# C3-b gate transient flake evidence (kept, not hidden)

## Default MCP client smoke (`src/ai-native/mcpClient.mts` "DEV advanced" step)

At ~22:15, after many parallel E2E/vitest/build runs, three consecutive cold
starts failed at the same pre-existing step:

  FAIL | DEV advanced timeout failed | {"ok":false,"code":"E_RETRYABLE","messageKey":"another advanced action is already in flight"}

Verification that this is NOT a C3-b regression:

1. Rebuilt `dist-mcp/mcpServer.mjs` with the ORIGINAL `git show HEAD:vite.mcp.config.ts`
   (single-entry `ssr: resolve(...)` config) and re-ran the same client:
   SAME failure, same step, same E_RETRYABLE. The C3-b dual-entry config is not
   the cause.
2. Root cause is a pre-existing race in `src/ai-native/sessions.ts`:
   `cancelAction()` sets `abort.aborted = true` synchronously but
   `advancedInFlight.delete(actionId)` happens later in the background loop's
   `finally`. A follow-up `game_execute_action` issued immediately after cancel
   can arrive before the slot is released.
3. Under lighter load, three consecutive independent cold starts all PASS:
   PASS | run1 | MCP client done
   PASS | run2 | MCP client done
   PASS | run3 | MCP client done
4. Final gate run `final_default_mcp_client.log`: PASS / MCP client done.

No assertion was changed, no timeout was relaxed, and `sessions.ts` was NOT
modified (C3-a semantics and the frozen unit suite stay intact).
The C3-b unit suite (454 tests) and the full 55/55 E2E suite are unaffected.

## Full E2E one-time failure (fixed in this round, not a flake)

  FAIL | full_e2e | ai-native-world.spec.ts:772 F-04/F-05 | Expected "HUMAN", got "CONTROL  PAUSED"

Cause: `PauseScene` instance fields (`controlText` / `externalStatusText`) kept
references to destroyed Text objects after `scene.restart()`; `update()` touched
them and broke the overlay's close tween.
Fix: reset all three label fields in the scene `shutdown` handler.
Re-verification: that spec 1/1 PASS, then full E2E 55/55 PASS twice.
